WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 3.6 · Structure, Governance & Accountability
Decision rights and delegation of authority

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
Write down who can approve what, up to which limit.

3
00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:15.600
1. Raise the approval level as the risk rises.

4
00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:18.200
2. Name who approves when someone is away or conflicted.

5
00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:22.200
3. Use the same limits in your finance procedures.

6
00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:23.800
An example: Vanita Weavers Cooperative (Cooperative · member-owned, India)

7
00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:31.000
“Vanita: Meera orders yarn up to US$2,000; a purchase subcommittee up to US$5,000; above that, the elected committee.”

8
00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:33.400
You create a delegation matrix with absence and conflict rules.

9
00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:37.400
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

10
00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:42.000
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
